# Negative-control mutant — the payment-method form on an active contract (AC-8, R13)
#
# RE-CUT (FE-3206): the `available.changingPaymentMethod.idle` `PAYMENT_METHOD`
#   transition now already carries `cond: "canChangePaymentMethod"`. The mutation
#   keeps its effect — it re-gates that transition to `isCancelling`, so an active
#   (non-cancelling) contract refuses the form. (Replaces the prior "add
#   isCancelling" form since the transition is no longer condless.)
#
# Scenario it must flip: contract.feature:380 "I change how my contract is paid
#   for through the payment-method form, whatever its standing", Examples row
#   active (feature:387).
# Test that goes red: contract.payment-method-standing.int.test.ts:185
#   "I change how my contract is paid for through the payment-method form,
#   whatever its standing" (the form never opens on the active capture, so
#   `expect(manager.useMeta().isPaymentMethodOpen.value).toBe(true)` flips).
#   Every other test that opens the form on the active capture goes red with it.
# Mutation: the `available.changingPaymentMethod.idle` `PAYMENT_METHOD`
#   transition is gated to `isCancelling`, so an active contract refuses the
#   form.
#
# Apply with:  git apply <this file>   (run from repo root)
# Revert with: git apply -R <this file>
diff --git a/packages/headless/src/modules/contract/contract.machine.ts b/packages/headless/src/modules/contract/contract.machine.ts
--- a/packages/headless/src/modules/contract/contract.machine.ts
+++ b/packages/headless/src/modules/contract/contract.machine.ts
@@ -140,9 +140,9 @@ export default createMachine(
               idle: {
                 on: {
                   PAYMENT_METHOD: {
                     target: "available",
                     actions: "setPaymentMethodSchemas",
-                    cond: "canChangePaymentMethod"
+                    cond: "isCancelling"
                   }
                 }
               },
